    details: "pg 3, col 6",
    sourceDate: "1868-12-22",
    summary: "Key figures including Mike McCoole and Bill Davis gathered at Fair Grounds, preparing for Davis's upcoming 19th-century boxing match against Tom Allen.",
    link: "http://statehistoricalsocietyofmissouri.org/cdm/ref/collection/dmr1/id/1681",
    localCopyEdited: "images/articles/image-003.jpg",
    localCopyFull: "images/articles/image-003b.jpg",
    id: "003",
    text: "A large number of the sports, including McCoole, Prendergast, Charlie Gallagher, Bill Ryall, Pat C. Conzallin, and others, went out to the Fair Grounds on Sunday to see Bill Davis, who is getting into condition for the fight with Tom Allen. Bill Davis is under the charge of Bill Blake alias “Dublin Tricks,” and Davis and his trainer were after a walk of 35 miles that day, when they met the lively Buck Sahe quarters at the gate of the grounds."
