    text: "Letween Tom Allen of St. Louis and Jem Mace, champion of England, will be described in next Sunday's Star. Told by Prof. Bill Clark to Billy Murphy. Pictures by George Grinham. No. 4 in the series of \"Great Stories of the Ring,\" now running in The Star, is a notable addition to ring history. Read of the scenes in New Orleans before the great battle, The St. Charles Hotel, the night before—Enthusiastic reception of the combatants—A fierce and bloody contest—Fearful punishment of the loser—Grand display of science by the winner, Tom Allen, the king of St. Louis. This story will be published in two parts—Part II, February 4."
