    id: "286",
    text: "ae\n\nTOM ALLEN AND JEM MACE\nSSS 2\n\nProbability of a Match Between Them\n\nThe last nmmber of the New York Clipper contain\nthe following tn relation to the proposed match betweai\nTom Allen and James Mace:\n\nThe plot thickens, and at present there is every nea\naon to believe that the 2 ey between Jim Mao\nand Tom Allen for a match, which may be od a\nhaving st issue the championship of the world, will re\nsult in a most satisfactory manner.\n\nAswe bave already slated, we telegraphed the sub.\nstance of Mace’s card, published in our last issue, tc\nAllen, and bright and early on the following morning\n(Dec. 28th) came an este Laat bs Tom stated that,\nas he was not aware what terms were, he was no!\ninclined to come to New York at the risk of having al\nhis journey for nothing in case they did not suit him,\nbut cee he would at onoe forward articles, ea mpanied\nby amouné requisite to cover Jim's ve\nhundred —-\n\nMace calle@@ our office during the day, accompanied\ny Sod cousin, Pooley, and his business manager, Fred.\n\nhams, and upon learning the contents of Tom’s\ntelegram was considerably yee ee poe as he thought\nhis offer was very fair, and professions! engagements\nwhich he could not break without great pecuniary loss\nrendered it out of the question for him to proceed te\nPittsburg before the lapse of a number of days, During\nthe Ans | he mailed the subjoined letter to Tom, the tenor\nof ich evinces his anxiety to effect a meeting with our\npresent champion. Read it:\n\"ee ic voety Se your ovadive...",
