    id: "298",
    text: "THE PRIZE RING.\nReposted Fight for $1,000 a Side. -\n\nAfiee ail the paper sparring lately between Bill\nDav's, the Calitornian champion, and Bill Ryall, of\nthis city, relative to getting up a match bet ween\nthem, the affair has “feli through,” as the sports\nsay. It is not for the want of pluck on the part of\ncitherof the champions that the arrangements for\nihe metch have not been perfected, and, as some\ncause must be assigned for the failure, those sports\nin the secret say that the ‘“‘spendulix couldn’t be |\nTix” to make it £2,500 a side.\n\nBat sooner than entirely disappoint the fistic tra-\nterpity of St. Louis, a match has been made between\nbill (Wiltiam M.) Davis, of California, and Tom Al-\nlen, of Cleveland, Ohio, both well-known pugilists\nwho have punished some smart men m their lay.\n\nOur sporting reperter went yesterday efter-\nnoop, a3 usual, among the sports to see\n“what was up.” He found about sixty er\nseventy-tive of the “pride of the prize ring” con-\nccegated im the sitting room of Bill Kyull’s saloon,\non Waching*on avenue, debating the Davis-Alien\nencounter proposed to ceme off.\n\nFrom bl Ryall’s, a large detachment! adjourned\nto Jack Looney’s “Butcher's Exchange.” Ryall\nand Davis formed # of the party, as Artemus\nWard would say. ly Pendegrass was elected\nChairman, and —— Harvey acted as writist of the\neS ele ee",
