    text: "THE COMING PRizE FiGut.—Among the sporting\nfraternity the chief item for discussion and wager\nis the approaching prize fight between Tom Allen\nand Charlie Gallagher, both of Cleveland, to come\noff on the 23d of this month.\n\nLast evening McCocle’s new house, opposite the\nCourt-Honse,was absolutely thronged with the fancy\nand those who take an interest in the “manly art of\nself-defence” to hear the reading of the articles of\nagreement and to witness the fina! deposit of $300 a\nside made into the hands of the stake-holder, Wil-\nliam Murray. Among the noted sports were Mike\nMcCoole and Charlie Gallagher, fightists; Dublin\nTricks, John Looney ard Tom Riley, backers; P.\nH.Connallm and Tom Kehoe. Enthusiasm was\nmanifested on both sides, but the betting ran rather\nslowly in favor of Allen. The greatest conviviality\nwas maintained, and the “flowing bow!” was drained\n“frequently and oft,” while amid a continual din\nrang the standing toast of “May the best man\nwin!” Allen looks in excellent condition, but Gal-\nlagher appears as it he was somewhat over-tralned.",
