    title: "Referee Declares Allen vs Gallagher Fight a Draw",
    localCopyEdited: "images/articles/image-359.jpg",
    localCopyFull: "images/articles/image-359b.jpg",
    id: "359",
    text: "THE LATE PRIZE FIGHT.\n\n \n\nA Meeting at the Ivy\n“Green. ~\n\n——_—_—__\n\nSTATEMENT OF THE REFEREE |\n\n——_—\n\nKELLY NON EST.\n\n \n\nA SUBSEQUENT MEETING\n\n \n\n|\n\nLooney Carries the Day.\n\n \n\nTHE FIGHT DECIDED A DRAW.\n\n \n\nALLEN HAS NO SHOW FOR FAIR PLAY |\nIN ST. LOUIS.\n\n \n\nAljen Challenges Gallagher. |\n\n—_\n\nIt was announced yesterday in the papers that Mr.\nWeesells, the referee in the late mill between Allen and\nGallagher, wou'd be at the ‘‘Ivy Green,” on Market\nstreet, at four o’clock yesterday afternoon, to hear the\nstatements of Kelly, the alleged sponge thrower, and\nothers who witnessed the fight, and give his final de-\ncision accordingly. An hour before the time named, an\nimmense crowd of the fancy assembled at the Ivy Green, |\nblocking up the sidewalk and making it necoseary for\nthe police to clear the way for foot passengers. Nearly\nall the pugilists of the city were in the vicinity, anxious\nto hear what the referee would say. —\n\nGallagher was there, but left before Wesselis arrived.\nHe was followed along the street. by a crowd of boys,\nwho looked upon him with as much awe and veneration\nas they would survey Dan Rice’s big elephant or a live\ngiraffe.\n\nCharley complained to our reporter that the Democrat\nhad done him injustice in saying that he struck spite-\nfully at Allen when the latter offered to shake hands\nwith him after the sponge was thrown up. He declared\npositively that he did not know that the sponge had been\nthrcwn up, and was ready to go on with the fight when\nAllen left...",
    summary: "The St. Louis Globe-Democrat reported on August 21, 1869 about the disputed decision between Tom Allen and Charley Gallagher. After hearing testimony about whether the sponge was thrown, Referee Larry Wessells declared the fight a draw.",
