    text: "THE LATE PRIZE FIGHT.\nAlien vs. Gallagher—A Card from Butt Riley.\n\nThe Cincinnati Enquirer ot Tuesday contains the\nfollowing card from Butt Riley, one of Allen’s sec-\nonds m the recent fight: ;\n\nCINCINNATI, A 1869,\nTo the Editors of the Enquirer: pet\n\nales pone one of Tom Allen’s seconds in his\nfight with Charlie Gallagher, un the 17th inst., I de-\nsire to correct some stateweuts that were mare In the\npublic prints regarding the atfuir. I was in a posi-\ntion to know what did occur, and will give you my\nstatement as briefly as possibile.\n\nIn the first four rounds the fighting was very\nhard and fast, neither having the best of it- us\nte the fourth round, Gallagher apparently le:\nAllen, but in the fifth round the tide was com-\npletely turned. In this round Allen hit Gallagher\nwhere, and as often as he wanted to, punishing nim\nseverely, and getting sway without a return. He\nseemed to be completely at the mercy of Allen, either\ngoing down to avoid punishment voluntarily, or be-\n\nep xueched down. This siate of affairs ¢ontinued\ntill the last round of the fight.\n\nWhen time was called for the last round, Alien\ncame up to the centre of the ring, and stow! waiting\nfor Gallagher, who was still sitting in his corner.\nAfter the lapse of twelve or fourteen seconds I tobi\nGallagher's seconds to bring their man out to the\n\n| scratch. Mr. Kelly, one of his seconds, walkel out\nfive or six paces from his corner, and threw up the\n| eee This was, 1 consider, a token of the defeat\nhis principal....",
