    text: "Tom Allen's Pronuuciamento.\nNew Onxteass, La., May 12, 18\nin regard to my recent encounter with M:\nMace, for #5,000 and the championship,\nbave tosay is thatI did my best to wi\nfriends’ money who backed me, and that I fe\nas well as I knew how to fight. Mace outfc\nmeand won, I was beat and. lost, and ha’\nexcuse to make: but everybody knows that\ncouldn’t win. In order to let the public see\nI am neither a cur nor a coward, I hereby\nto fight any man in the °\n(bar the champion of the world, Jom Mace\nJ. C. Heenan), for from #500 to 85,000. I:\nmore especially Joe Coburn, Mike McCoole, |\nley Gallagher, Joe Goss, or anbody, barrin;\nabove two gentlemen. I will fight Cobur\nfrom $500 to $5000, and would sooner fight\nor Joe Goss tham any man breathing. I\nbusiness, and hope that some of these woul\nfighters will at once put up a forfeit and shos\nmean business. This challenge stands ope\nthree months, so that these fighters can\npi Saeed to make a match.\nmy fight with Mr. James Mace he k\ngave me the title of champion, which he w:\ndefeating me, and expressed a determinatio\ndid J. C. Heenan, that he would never enté\nprize ring again. Iaccepted Mr. Mace's |\ntook back the title af champion which I had\nand, with my life, strength, and endurat\nam prepared to defend that title against all\nera, bairing Mr. Mace and Mr. Heenan. .\nturn thanks to the sporting fraternity all ov\ncountry for their hind support. | Tom Aur\n| Champion of Am:",
