    text: "Mace and Alien Punching Each Other's\nHee2ds in the Tammeany—Tom’s Claim\nof the Chemprenship—The Coming\nContest with Mike McCoole.\n\n{From the New York Sun. June 18 J\nThe Hon. Jem Mace and his Excellency Tom Allen\nbad a sparring match last evening in Tammany. Both\nare about 37 years of age, and five feet nine in height.\n\nThey wore tight-fitting shirts of white elastic cotton, .\n\nwhite knee breeches, white stocking, and white box-\n\ning gloves. Both had cropped hair, of ceurse. Jem\nbad a frame ¢eveloped to ite full capabliity, but with-\nout a particle of superfiuous flesh. Tom is a smasher,\nand carries extra beef. He inclines to a corporation,\nand bas bard work to keep it down. The gentlemen\n. were intrednced by a venerable usher in a black even-\n\ning suit. He remarked thet as Jem had retired from\nthe prize sing since bis last battle, Tom was the cham-\npion of Amesica, apd had challenged all apponents,\nMike McCoole, he said, was soon to contest the cham-\npionship with him, for $5000 a side. He then exhibited\nthe champion’s belt held by Tom, and a beit presented\nto Jem by his New York friends. The eentestant\nsports then fought four rounds, and then the gloves\n‘flopved ——— on mugs and bread baskets. Jem\nshowed wonderful agility. He danced about as thouzh\nbe bad won a £100,000 lottery prize, He ducked, aud\nbobbed, and wriggied, and digged, and > Tom\netood firm in ope spot, and let cut some shots from the\nthc ulder that would bave knocked Jem through the\nwall into the street if he...",
