    text: "The undersigned, a committee appointed by the\ncounty court to assist the U.S. marshal m obtaining\na full and complete report of the population and in-\ndustrial resources of our city and county, respectfully\nbat mest urgently call upon the citizens of St. Louis\ncounty te make full and complete returns to the\ncenses-takers. The census of L860 did great injustice\nto St. Louis for the reason that many, through a false\nconception, refused to furnish the information asked\nfor. An impression seems to prevail that information\ngiven in Tegard to business or property will be made\nuse of by the assessors in the collection of taxes. We\nbeg to disabese the minds of our citizens on this point.\nThe information thus obtained is held as confidential\nand is reported and published only im aggregates, and\ncan in no way be made nse of by the assessors. We\nfeel that our city has become the great central point\nin the Mississippi valley, and is now increasing in\npopulation, wealth and manufactures faster than any\ncity west of the Alleghanies, and it is ofthe utmost\nimportance to its future destiny that the present cen-\nsus shall be correctly and fully taken in order that St.\nLouis may obtain ber proper place in the list of the\ngreat cities of the United States.\n\nWe append a list of questions asked, and\nwould request heads of families to prepare the\nanswers and leave the same at their residences\nto be delivered when called for, our sister cities are\nstraining every nerve to outstrip us, and we...",
