    text: "ACCIDENTAL SHOOTING.\nMan Killed im Tom Allen’s Saloon by the\nProprietor.\n\nA young man named Nelson Adams came to his\ndeath yesterday morving by the accidental dis-\ncharge of a pistol, in the house of Tom Allen, the\npugilist.\n\n| The tragedy occurred at the latter's saloon, on\n\nWashington avenue, near Fifth street, about\neve o'clock. Allen and Adams were talking together\nabout fire-arms, the former maintaining that the\nEnglish patiern waa the best, and in order to ex-\nplain the matter, according to Ailen's statement, the\nthe latter pniled out his pistol, and Adams, being\nrather full at the time, made a grab at the Weapon,\nand as Allen pulled back it went off, the ball pene-\ntrating the abdomen. Tae unfortanate man feil\never on the counter where heleaned. When the\nterrible result was fully reatized, Allen it appears |\nran for a physician and also called in the police. Tae\nyoung man lived but an bour and fire minutes.\nHe spoke only one werd between the time the fatal\nstot struck him and his disolution. When told by\nacompanion, “ Reddy you are shot,” he answered\n“Yes.” The inquest was;eeld attne Third district\nstation. The biood oozed from the wound oa\nthe lower right side of the abdomen,\nThe pistol was a_ silver-mounted Derringer ef\nEvglish pattern. Tom Allen entered the room, tol-\nlowed by a group of trrends, and appeared amch af-\ntected as he gazed at the dead maa, the victim of\nbis own band, q\n\nThe toltowing is the testimony of two of the most\nimportant witnesses:\n\nTESTIMONY...",
