    text: "ee ee te eee Bote tee eed ee\nTHE CHAMPION.\n\nReturn of Tom Allen—He Brings an Hlé-\ngent Preseut from Philadelphia—W hat\ne Says About the Falked.of Mill with\nRook, }\nTom Allen, the belted pugilist of Ameriea, re-\n\nturned home yesterday from a visit to the princi-|\npal cities of the East. He gave sparring exhibi-\ntions in. New York, Boston, Philadelphia, and\nPittsburg, and was everywhere received with en-!\nthusiasm by large crowds of his admirers. j\nAt Philadelphia Tom was presented, on the oc-\ncasion of his benefit, with a large solid silver\ngoblet, holding a quart, tastefully chased and en-\n\ngraved, and bearing the following inscription:\n\n“Presented to Tom Allen, Champion of Amegica,\n\ne his numerous eee sien friends, at J. M. |\n\nik Grand Central Variety Theater, March\n\nOn the side opposite the inscription is engraved\naroped arena, with two “scrapers” in the act of:\nmauling each other. ae top, oF cover, 18 sur-\nmounted by the figure of a gladiator, The vessel\ncost $250. :\n\n' In regard to the mill announced to'come off with\nRook in June, Tom says he thinks his opponent\nwill forfeit,as Rook is ‘no greatscratch.” He did\nnot see Rook at the time stated by the Sun, but\nthat chicken came to one of his exhibitions. Allen\nis in fine health, but still quite fleshy. He will.\nleave the city intwo or three weeks and go into\ntraining. i",
