    text: ". ee ee ee a OT Te rele Ey EE J\nIt WONT WORK, |\nThe Latest Scheme Put Up on Tom\n\nAllen by Disappointed New York-—\n\ners.\n\nYesterday afternoon a representative of this pa- —\nper dropped into the ‘‘Champion’s Rest,” on Waslt- |\nington avenue, where he found Tom Allen, the\npugilist, enjoying a good cigar and complaining of\nthe heat. The object of the reporter was to as-\ncertain what the statement going the rounds of\nthe press, to the effect that Jem Mace, the scien-\ntific gypsy, had accepted his challenge, meant.\nThrough that reporter the public will be posted in\nregard the latest job thathas been put up on the\nfamous knight of the fives, who has made St,\nLonis his home. The New Yorkers, who hate\nAllen as they do poison, for the “reason that they\ncannot handle him, and are disgusted at being un-\nable tofind any one who can best the stalwart\nBritisher in the roped arena, spread a report\nto the effect that he had challenged Mace,\nin order to bring Jem out. Not satisfied with this,\nthey circulated the rumor that Mace had accepted,\nin order that Tom might be heard from. The\nseheme won’t work. Mace and Allen understand\neach other, and while the former is aware that\n‘Tom has retired, the latter desires to strengthen\nthat opinion by the assertion that he will never\nagain enter the squared circle.\n\nEd. O’ Baldwin, the Irish giant, who has just\nserved a term in the Pennsylvania Penitentiary, is\ndesirous that Allen should travel with him and\ngive sparring exhibitions throughout the...",
