    localCopyFull: "images/articles/image-526b.jpg",
    id: "526",
    text: "‘A telegram from New York states that a_\nmatch is made and forfeit up for a fight be\ntween Tom. Allen and Jem. Mace. It is\nabout time that these old men were prepar\ning todie. If the “ring™ is not played’ out,\nlet the fuct be shown by trotting out some\nyoung men with modern ideas of the busi-—\nness. The English prize ring has been a_\nfraud and a humbug—both in theory and\npractice—from its earliest history to the\nlast brutal exhibition of its principles. It\nwas not established in the true spirit of\nscicnee. and the practice under it has shown\nit to be au means of brutal exhibitions of en- |\ndurance little less atrocious than needless\nbutchery. When Allen, Mace, McCool, and\nthe rest of this generation of fighters are\nbattered off the face of the earth, it is to be\nhoped a new degree will be established in\nthe ‘‘manly art of self-defense,” judged by\nwhich no fighter or boxer will be allowed\n| fo inure an antagonist when down nor to\n| touch him standing other than with his fist,\n\nin biows or feints. The present system that\n| permits clinching and throwing would dis-\n| grece a combat of grizzly bears. and a>\nJeng as it prevails the prize ring will be a\n| disgrace to humanity.",
