    id: "530",
    text: "SK =\n'\n| FISTIC HONORS.\n| Siete)\nThe Proposed Mill for the Champion-\nship of the World.\n\nWhat Allen Has to Say on the Subject--The Mace\nProgramme--A Fight in the Indian Terri-\ntory Not Improbable\n\nThe Eastern press, as well as numerous journals\nin the West, which dabble periodically in ring\nmatters, publish sensational dispatches at inter-\nvals to the effect that an international prize-fight\nis on the tapis, and that the fistic gladiators whe\n\nare to face each other for the championship and\na good round sum are none other than Jem Mace,\nthe scientific gypsy, and Tom Allen, who hae for\nsome years made St. Louishishome. These re-\nports haying gained some credence, a GLOBE:\nDmrMOcRAT reporter yesterday called upon Allen\nto see whether there was any truth in them, and\nfound that there was not.\n‘*TRICKS THAT ARE VAIN’’\nare practiced by certain members of the pugilistie\nfraternity in other ways than when opposed to an\nopponentin the squared circle, and the late ru-\nmnors Can be attributed to this fact. In England\nthe prize ring is an institution of the past, and\nsoon will be in this country. This fact is well\nknown to Mace, and his recent efforts to induce\nAllen to commit himself in aceepting his chal-\nes 4 are due to it. There is os money te be\nmade in his line across the water, but in this\ncountry there is, and in this way. His challenge\nto Allen will, of course, stir up a good deal of ex-\ncitement, as-itis.conceded that if the wmill was\nought on its merits a rare display of...",
