    id: "533",
    text: "TOM'’S TRAINER.\nMimic Battles Fought by Amateurs—A\nPleasing Private Entertainment.\n\nA grand complimentary benefit, of a private\nnature, was tendered to Ned. Donnelly by the\nmembers of Tom Allen’s Gymnasium Club, last\nnight, and the aitendance was quite flattering to.\nthe scientific young exponent of the manly art\nwho trained the champion for his fight with Geo.\nRooke, out of which the latter sneaked. In ad-\ndition to the scholars, several experts from the\nMissouri Gymnasium volunteered their services\nfor the occasion. The sparring wae first-class,\nthe scholars doing their teacher and themselves\ngreatcredit. The bout between George Nagle\nand Aleck Mann was a reid one, the\nlade slugcing away to their hearts’ con\ntent. Dnt and O'brien indulged in a\ngive-and-take affair, with the gloves, which was\nalso appreciated. Jack Madden faced the **Gyp-\npy.’’ and this pair, after exchanging fistic com-\npliments to the delight of the spectators, were\nfollowed by Tom Allon, who made things right liveiy\nforthe beneficiary, who proved, however, that\nhe knew how to save his head and hit hard. Hav\nne ao together before, young Donneily and\nthe champion exhibited the beauties of the art in\n2 eS manner, and the science dis-\naay ed by both was greeted with cnthusiastic ap-\n\nause.\n\nAmong the attractions of the evening was a\nfinely executed Ce garetet pass en.’ actby Mr. Charles\nstandbrook, who undoubtedly takes rank with\nthe best amateurs in the country. Collar and\nelbow wrestling was also a feature...",
