    text: "AGAIN VICTORIOUS.\n———__\nProf. Bauer Beats the German Champion\n! .\n| at His Own Game.\n\nA Splendid Exhibition of Strength and\nSkill at the Temple Last Evening.\n——\n\nThe second wrestling match between Prof.\nBauer and Herr Heygster for $250 aside came\noff last night at the Temple before a crowded\nhouse. There was considerable excitement\nManitest on accountot the terms of the match,\nwhich were thatthe first fallssould be wres-\ntled for according to German andthe second\naccording to Greco-Roman rules. It was be-\nlieved that this would give Heyysterthe ad-\n‘Vantage, because the German style is mainly\nanu exhibition of strength, und there is no\ncoubt regarding his superiority in this respect\nto Bauer, who relics in a great measure upon\n| his skill ane activity. 4\n| Tom Allen,the champion pugilist, introduced\nthe men to the audience at twenty-three min-\nutes past § o’clock. Leon Schuler appearing as\numpire’ for Bauer and Carl Boehm tor Heyg-\nster.\n| Atthe start the contestants forget that the\nfirst bout was uccording to German rules, and\n| had to make afreshstart. They began by a\nseries of wrist grips, which were continued tun-\ntil Heygster got a left arm body hold on Baner,\nwhen he tried hard to get both arms around\nhis body and secure a lock, but Bauer turned\nthe tables on him, and gained the very lock\nHeygster was striving for. He lost it, how-\never, and some very clever marncuvring wus\ndone, Heygster at length setting\n2 very good body hoid, which\nBauer broke by main strength =...",
