    id: "542",
    text: "; The Wrestlers.\n\nProf. Theobaud Bauer, the great wrestler, his\nestimable wife, Signor Andre Christol, Tom Allen\nand Mr. Leon Schuler, were yesterday the gucsts\nof Monsicur Jean Bonnet, the French caterer,\nwho was anxious to give his friends from La Belle\nFrance one more reminder of the estimation in\nwhich they are held by the people of St. Louis.\nAfter eséorting the party through the corridors of\nthe new Merchants’ Exchange and showing thea\nhow business was transacted in that edifice,\n\n| AN ELEGANT BREAKFAST\n\nwas partaken of in one of the private apartments\ntttached to the restaurant. When the delicacies\nhad been disposed of, Monsieur Bonnet grew en-\nthusiastic over the successes of his country in St.\nLouis, and reverted to thirty years ago, when, for\nive successive seazons he himself was recognized\nis the champion amateur wrestler of New Orleans\nund vicinity. All present thoroughly enjoyed |\nthemselvea.\n\nOn Sunday night the subjoined challenge was\nbanded the GLOBE-DEMOCEAT reporter, as a\nnews item; but, for obvious reasons, it was sent\nto the countipg-room, and appeared as an adver-\npisement: ‘\n\nSCHROEDER'S DEFI.\n\n‘*Although not being a professional wrestler, I\nhereby challenge the conqueror of the Oak of the\nRhine, Mons. T. H. Bauer, to wrestle with me\naceording to the ‘German Rules of Wrestling,’\nfor any amount of money the gentleman may\nplease to name.\n\n**Respectfully,” JULIUS SCHRRODER,\n\n‘*Proprietor Section Eleven, Fifth and Myrtle\nstreets.\n\n**St. Louis, April 9,...",
