    text: "THE SPORTING WORLD.\nBauer and Sthroeder to Wrestie on\nSaturday Night Week—Probability\n\nof a Match with Coburn—Tom Al-\n\nlen’s Match with Joe Goss, the Eng-\nlish Champion.\n—_— >_>\n\nAt three o’clock yesterday afternoon Prof.\nThiebaud Bauer, the Greco-Roman wrestler,\nmet Julius Schroeder, proprietor of **Section\n11°* saloon at Tony Faust’s, where arrange-\nments Were made fora match to come off on\nSaturday, May 6, atthe Temple. if that hall\nean be secured, or at some other place\nto be duly «announced in ease the\nTemple is engaged. Since the recent\nmatches between Bauer and Hevester, the\n**Oak of the Rhine,** who, by the way, de-\nfeated Christol at Chicago, on Tuesday even-\ning, Schroeder Tas been agai anxious to\nwrestie the Alsatian. They hada meeting\nseveral days ago, when a forfeit of $100 a\nside Was put up. Yesterday thix amount was\nincreased to $250 a side, the balance to be\nfortheoming on Thursday next, three days\nbefore the match, and the party not appear-\ning iu person or by his representative with\nthe balance of the stakes to forfeit all. Bauer\nWas represented yesterday by Fred. Wat-\nkins, and Schroeder by Mr. John F.\nVogel. There was considerable trouble in\ncoming to terms, Schroeder insisting on\nhaving the first fall German style, the second\naccording to Greco-Roman rules, and the\nthird, if necessary to decide the best two out\nof three, according to German rules. Bauer,\non the other hand, wanted to toss for the\nchoice of a third fall, but finally yielded the\npoint to...",
