    text: "THE PRIZE RING.\n\nJoe Goss Issues a Business| Challenge to\nTom Allen to Fight for Any Amount\nof Money.\n\n(From the Cincinnati Enquirer pf Yesterday.)\n\nThere is now a4 good prospect for a rattling mill\nbetween Joe Goss and Tom Allen. Mr. Eph Hol-\nland, a perfectly reliable business man, yesterday\nreceived a letter from Joe Goss, who is now in\nNew York with Howe & Cushing!s Circus, Inclos-\ning a draft for $500 and the following emphatic\nchallenge:\n\n*“*‘New York, April M4, 1876.—Mr. Thos. Allen,\nChampion of Ameriea: 1 heretiy challenge you\nto fight meina 9 hg Ff foot ring, according\nto the rules of the London prize ring, for any\namount of money ftom $500 to) $5,000 a side and\nthe Chasaplonstia of the world. |The time, place\nof meeting aud final stakeholder to be hereafter\nagreed upon. To show that I inean business, I\nhave this day forwanted to Mr. Eph Holland. 101\nWest Fifth strect, Cincinnati, O.|, thesum of $500,\nand, ss soon as you shal! have cavered it, I will at\nonce go to that city and meet n or your repre-\nsentatives to make final apengoweste: The New\n\n’ York sporting papers having declined to publish a\nchallenge addressed to you, 1 have forwarded this\nto the Cincinnati Xnguirer, with\\a request to pub-\nlieh it. bes 5 wy te ge &\n«*Joxe Goss, Champion of England.’’\n\nChicago and St, Louis papers ane copy. ;\n\nThis bas the ring of business about it, and evi-\ndently is notintended for inere buncombe. Allen\nhas had some personal altercations both with the\nNew York Nope and...",
