    title: "Tom Allen Acts as Stakeholder in Wrestling Match Between Bauer and Schroeder",
    localCopyEdited: "images/articles/image-552.jpg",
    localCopyFull: "images/articles/image-552b.jpg",
    id: "552",
    text: "Tho Wrestlers. ,\n\nThe final arrangements for the wrestling match\nbetween Prof. Bauer and Herr Julius Schroeder\nwere completed yesterday afternoon, at Tony\nFaust’s, when the remaining $250 a side was ad-\nvanced, making the stakes, as they now stand,\n$500 a side, or an even $1,000, ;\n\nMr. Schroeder appeared@.in company with his\nfriend and umpire, J. F. Vogel, but Bauer was\nnot present. He wag represented, however, by\nTom Allen, who was authorized to act for him and\ndeposit the remainder of the money.\n\nThe pugilist was also duly empowered to sign\narticles of agrecment and make any necessary ar-\nrangements. Leon Schuler was also present, pre:\npared to turn over the $500 already up, providing\nhis functions as stakeholders should ‘cease. In\nAddition to these, several well-known sporting\nmen were present, one of whom was prepared\nwith plenty of money to back Bauer against Co-\nburn; but,as none of the friends of the latter gen.\ntleman came to time, it is presumed that they are\nnot anxious for a match,\n\n_ The party were accommodated with a private\nroom, and Tom Allen promptly drew out a couple\nof bills with a big ‘'C’’ In the corner, and a fifty,\nand called upon Schroeder to coyer it. The Ger-\nman had come ag and in an instant Li:\npile was laid down ide the other, and articles\nof agreement drawn up and signed. The match\nis totake place to-morrow evening at the Tem.\nle, and from every indication that hall will be\nmmed, so anxious do the sporting fraternits\nseem to be as to the result....",
