    id: "559",
    text: "One More Defeat.\n\nNew HaveN, June 9.—New Havens, 7; St.\nLouis Browns, 5. ‘\n\nPITTSBURG, June 9.—Philadelphis, 5; Alle-\nghenys, 1.\n\nMace and Goss.\n(From the London Sporting and Dramatic N 5\nStay 2.1 ac\n\n**Those renowned pugilists, Mace and Goss,\nwho are at present on a tour with Howes & Cush-\ning’s Great Hippodrome, are causing quite a\nfurore in America. We learn (says the Sporting |\nLife) that the $500 deposited by Goss in the hands\nof Eph. Holiand, of Cincinnati, to make s mateh\nto fight Tom Allen, of St. Lonis, for the cham-\npionship of that country and a puree of frum $1,000\nto $5,900 has been covered by Allen, anda fight\nwill come off in about a month's time.’’ We take\nleave to predict that the fight will not come off\neither in a month's or at any othertime. Either |\nGoss will fail sick or Allen will feel an umeonquer-\nable yearning for a change of air, or the authori- |\nties willinterfere. But wipes, Me Great Hippo- |\ndrome will go on, and the pugt istic nae of the\nexhibition continue to draw so long as A makes\npublic announcements of his determination to\nfight Allen. |",
