    id: "561",
    text: "THE THUMPERS.\nJoe Goss and Tom Allen at Thoir Train-\ning Quarters.\n‘\nCurrent Gossip Concerning the Fight for\nthe Championship.\n\nThe fight which isto take place in September\nfor a big bundle anu the championship of Amer-\nica, between those noted exponents of the fistic\nart, Tom Allen and Joe Goss, continues to create\nmuch comment in sporting circles, and opinion is\npretty evenly dividea as to whether the ‘‘mill’’ is\nto be decided on its merits, or whether it-is a\nneatly put-up job to lure the unwary into paying\nsteep prices for excarsion tickets to witness a\nsham battle in which one or the other of the prin-\ncipals will at the proper moment acknowledge\nhimself vanquished.\n\nThe match was broughtabout in a rather peculiar\nway. It appears that wigile Mace was sojourning\nin England, prior to.his last visit to America, the\nreport gained credence that Allen was so very fat\nthat it would be an utter impossibility for him to\nagain get in condition to fight. Mace, who is as\nshrewd as he is clever with his fists, thought that\nit would be a good idea to match Goss against\nAllen, and as Joe had never been to this country,\nshould the match be made he would ‘prove a pay-\ning card in the way of sparring exhibitions.\n\nNEGOTATIONS\nwere entered into, and as Allen was anxious to\nhave ashy at his old antagonist, with whom he\nhad fought a draw in three rings, there was very\nlittle difficalty in coming to terms, and when the\nmen met at Cincinnati, for the purpose of draw- |\ning up articles, the...",
