    text: "ee ee ee\nGoss and Allen.\n[From the Cincinnati Enquirer. }\n\nIn deference to the request of the Society\nfor the Prevention of Cruelty to Animals,\nProsecuting Attorney Baker has made Joe\nGoss and Tom Allen give good and sufiicient\nbonds to keep the peace inthe state of Ohio\nfor one year. The law against prize-tighting\nis very stringent in this state, and neither\nGoss nor Alien ever had any idea of violating\nit. It is now authoritatively an-\nnounced that it has been determined\nto place the price of tickets to the\npugilistic excursion at seven dollars each\ninstead of ten dollars, as at firstintended. As\nbut a limited number willbe sold, and those\nto proper parties, those who wish to see the\nbig mili will do well to make early applica-\ntion for their pasteboard to Eph. Holland.\nThe fizhting ground has been selected, and\nis surrounded by a2 natural amphitheatre that\nwill enable all to have a full view of the ring\nwithout any crowding.\n\n———Ss aS",
