    localCopyEdited: "images/articles/image-572.jpg",
    localCopyFull: "images/articles/image-572b.jpg",
    id: "572",
    text: "THE BIG FIGHT.\nBattle Ground.\n\nJack Looney and His Mob\nDetermined to Have\nTom Whipped.\nALLEN’S “DUKES” ARE THE\nHARDEST, BUT HIS\nCHEEKS ARE\nSOFT.\n\nJoe Coburn Deelares Goss Must\nHave the Money, Although\nAllen’s the Best Man.\nGoes will Strip at 164 Pounds,\nand Allen at 178.\nVERY LATEST FROM THE\nFRONT.\n\nSpecial to the St. Louis Dispatch. |\n\nCrncrnmnati, Sept. 6.—The arrange-\nments for the great fight between Joe\nGoss and Tom. Allen have been com-\npleted, and Alien has already left for the\nfighting ground. Goss will follow at 3\no’clock this p. m.\n\nDad Ryan of St. Louis has been agreed\nupon as referee, and it is thought he\nwill agree toserve. Allen will be sec-\nonded by Tom Kelly of St. Louis and\nArthur Chambers of Philadelphia. Goss\nwill be seconded by Jem Mace and Joe\nCoburn.\n\nGoss will fight at about 164 pounds\nand Allen at about 178 pounds.\nWhile both men are in splendid\ncondition, Goss seems to be\nthe hardest. Allen’s hands are the\nhardest, but there is a softness on the\ncheek bones that his training has failed\nto take away, and heavy blows on his\npeepers will be liable to close them and\nblind him. .\n\nThe fight promises to be along and\ndesperate one.\n\nJack Looney of St. Louis, and a party\nof 25 men arrived this morning. They\nsay that Allen must be whip-\nped, but they will not re-\nsort to any unfair means to accom-\nplish that end. Joe Coburn says\nthat while he considers Allen the\nbetter man, he (Allen) is bound to\nlose the fight. It looks like this, Ac-\ncording to Coburn,...",
