    text: "stopped at the end of the seventh round\n\nby the militia,\n\nFirst Blood and First Kaeck-Down\nFor Allen,\n\nCincinnati, Sept. 7.—Goss is the\nworst punished of the two men at the\nend of the seventh round. Firzt blood\nand first knock-down for Allen. Pros-\npect that the fight will be renewed ia\nanother place.\n\nThe Fight.\n\nCrncrynati, Sept. 7.—The point\nchosen for the tight between Allen and\nGoss is Cloverfield, near Walton, Ken-\ntucky, on the Louisville Short Line\n\nRailroad, eighteen miles from Cincin-\nnati. Acrowd of some 500 were ir at-\ntendance. Goss and Allen take their |\nplaces\n\nIn the Ring\nAt seven o'clock. The fight begins at\n7:35. Goss first steps to the middle of\nthe ring.\n\nFirst Round—Both men spar cauti-\nously, Goss falling into Allen’s corner.\nThe sparring is rather tiresome for the\ncrowd.\n\nFirst Blood for Allen,\nAnd a clinch and a fall, Goss on top.\nTime, seven minutes.\n\nSecond Round—Allen strikes Goss on\nthe lips and slightly staggers him. Goss\nhas given Allen some heavy body\nblows. Goss’ mouth bleeding. A fall\nfor Alien.\n\nThird Round—Close fighting. Allen\nwinning.\n\nAt this point\n\nThe Militia Appeared,\nBut the fighting goes on.\n\nCapt. Frank Wood, with the Coving-\nton Light Guards, reached the point\nnorth of Walton at 7 o’clock, having\nbeen carried past the fighting grounds\nby the conductor. Capt. Wood stopped\nthe train three miles past the point, and\nthe militia marched back, arriving at 8\no'clock.\n\nFourth Round—Exchanges fast and\nheavy. Allen, by a terrible blow...",
