    text: "s THOMAS ALLEN.\nHis Arrival in St. Louis and Reception\nby Friends.\n— -\nHow He Looks and Talks--No More P. R.\nfor Him.\n\nTom Allen is back. The man who licked Joe\nGoss, and who was cheated out of a fair fight by\n\nthe New York delegation that bet on Goss, ar-\n\nrived in our city yesterday morning, and, from all\naccounts, will make his home here henceforward.\nDuring the day he visited his many friends, who\nwere anxiously awaiting. his return. Those who\nbaunt Tom Kelly's saw him first, and after that\nhe looked in at Jim Gayin’s, at Charley Henry’s,\nand one or two other places, taking his dinner at\nthe Olive Street, where he isa registered, by the\nway. In the evening he visited the Comique, and\nwas waited on by all the boys. It was a shake of\nthe hand with this one, a little chat with another,\n8 drink with the third, a private confab with the\nnext, and a square talk with the GLoBE-DEMoO-\nCRAT reporter.\n\n. HOW DOES ALLEN LOOK?\n\nHe looked the very picture of physical health.\nHair just cropping out again, showing the gray,\nhowever, a fact noticed by his friends. Nota\nsign of punishment on his face, which is just be-\nginning to show the ‘‘moss’’ of a mustache, and\nthe first outgrowths of whiskers and beard. Lips\nenregle. Hands O. K., the mght one holding a\ngold-headed cane. Tom wore a dark hat, dark\nfrock-coat, light pants, cut close. You couldn’t\nhelp noticing his small feet. Present weight, 180\nponnas.\n\nThere was little about him to betray the pugilist.\nA certain sans souct alr...",
