    text: "THE FISTIC ART.\nAn Account of the Allen-Gilbert\nGlove Fight by Rounds.\n,\nThe Mill Too One-Sided to Be Interesting--Gale\n‘ the Cardiff Pedestrian’s, Latest Perform-\n‘ ance--Sporting Squibs.\n\nThe London Sporting Life, of October 31, con-\ntaing the best account of the glove fight between\nTonmmAllen and Tompkin Gilbert for the English\nchampionship yet published. Both were greeted\nwith applause, and the principals, in accordance\nwith custom, having shaken hands at 8:45,\n‘‘Time’’ was called, and the men threw them-\nselyes into position, and the battle commenced.\n\nTHE FIGHT BY ROUNDS.\n\nRound 1—As soon as the seconds stepped aside,\nthe men came up with great readiness, Gilbert\nwho appeared very anxious, leading off on ar\nlen’s face with his left, and be followed this up\nwith another, ever phd in retura heavily on the\neye. This nettled Gilbert, and he rushed in at\nAllen, and received a fair ‘‘crusher’’ full on the\nnose, Causing the blood to flow profusely. Allen\ndid not follow his advantage up, but waited until\nGilbert recovered himseif, and then let him have\nanother hot-’un on the jaw, which made the\nLincoln man wince. Some merry exchanges fol-\nJowed, Allen repeatedly visiting the face and Gil-\nbert the body, and arally inthe latter's corner\nWas ail in favor of Alien, who at the termination\nslung out his left heavily on Giiberi’s head, the\nforce of which sent him down. Time, 4 min. 10\nsec.\n\nRound 2—Gilbert was upto time, again bent\non forcing the fighting, for which he got...",
