    text: "Pedestrians and Pugilists.\n\nNew York, Oct. 30.—At a meeting of the\npedestrians of last week’s contest, the Man-\nagement announced the receipts were $26,373,\nand expenditures $21,443,leaving a balance of\n$4,299, less 15 per cent., which went to the\nmanagement. This left $998 and stakes to be\ndivided. Fitzgerald received $3,649; Nore-\nmac, $1,149, Herty, $599. Hughes retused\nto take his award or $99.\n\nRichard.K. Fox has deposited with Harry\nHiil $1,000, and issued a challenge, offering\nto back Tem Allen, ex-champion of America,\nto fight any pugilist, John 8S. Sullivan pre-\nferred, for the championship ot the world and\n$1,000 to $2,500 a side, within 100 miles of\nNew Orleans, within three months after sign-\ning articles.",
