    text: "The Ring.\nSULLIVAN AND ALLEN.\nTSpecial Dispatch to the Enquirer.]\n\nNew YorK, November 12.—In sporting so-\nciety itis believed that a match for $5,000, be-\ntween Tom Allen, of England, and John L.\nSullivan, of Boston, will soon be made. Allen\nrecently issued a challenge to fight Sullivan for\nthe championship of the world,. and Richard\nK. Fox, Allen’s backer, deposited $1,000 with\nHarry Hill to prove that Allen desires to fight.\nSullivan has informed Hill that he will be in\nNew York on the 20th inst. and will sign arti-\ncles of agreement to fight Allen. Tlre_latter is\neager to regain the title of champion, which\nhe held from 1870 to 1876, when Goss won the\ntitle through the dealing of a fonl blow by\nAilen. Sullivan has sent word to Mr. Fox that\nhe will fight Allen for $5,000 a side, or for any\nsum that gentieman can raise, the battle to\ntake place in Colorado orin the Indian Terri-\ntory, where there will be no police interfer-\nence.",
