    text: "The Union Ciub’s Tournament.\n\nThe bicycle and athletic tournament which is to\ntake place at the Union Base-Ball Grounds on July\n4 is now attracting the full attention of the sporting\nfraternity. The affair wil! be by iong odds the best\nof the kind ever given in the West. By to-morrow\nmorning the fifth of a mile cinder track, which is to\ncircle the grounds, will be completed, and the sur-\nface will be made as level as the top of a billiard\ntable. ‘The biecyele race for the Anheuser-Busch\nChallenge Cup will be run on this, and as there are\nseveral entries, the race will be disposed of in heats,\neight or ten men starting at a time. The sprinting\nand running matches will also be disposed of on this\ncourse. Next in point of importance to the bicycle\nrace will be the sparring matches, which are to take\nplace in a regular twenty-four-foot ring,\nthe colers of the various candidates being\ntied to the stakes. The best of the local sper\nrers promise to compete for the heavy, the middle\nand the light weight prizes. Soft blackened gioves\nwill be used, and the work af each competitor wil!\n\nbe judged ot by the number of points he scores\nsat his opponents head, face and body. After the\nyoungsters have had their fun, the veterans, Tom\n‘Allen and Tam Kelly, wil! appear and do the wind-\nup, while another attraction in this line will be the\n| Sppeetence of Frank and George Williams, aged 7\nand © years, and who are the cleverest youns box-\nersinibe world. All whotake part in these en-\ncounters...",
