    text: "The Union Ciub’s Tournament.\n\nThe bicycle and athletic tournament which is to\ntake place at the Union Base-Ball Grounds on July\n4 is now attracting the full attention of the sporting\nfraternity. The affair will be by long odds the best\nof the kind ever given in the West. By to-morrow\nmorning the fifth of a mile cinder track, which is to\ncircle the grounds, will be completed, and the sur-\nface will be made as level as the top of a billiard\ntable. The bicyele race for the Anheuser-Busch\nChallenge Cup will be run on this, and as there are\nseveral entries, the race will be disposed of in heats,\neight or ten men starting ata time. The sprinting\nand running matches will also be disposed of on this\ncourse. Next in point of importance to the bicycle\nrace will be the sparring matches, which are to take\nplace in a _ regular twenty-four-foot ring,\nthe colors of the various candidates being\ntied to the stakes. The best of the local pats\nrers promise to compete for the heavy, the mi dle\nand the light weight prizes. Soft blackened gloves\nwill be used, and the work of each competitor will\nees of by the numberof points he scores\n\ns ma, mene head, face and body. After the\n\nyoungsters nave had their fun, the veterans, Tom\n‘Allen and Tom Kelly, will appear and do the wind-\nup, while another attraction in this line will be the\nSopeeriece of Frank and George Williams, aged 7\nand © years, and who are the cleverest_ youns box-\nersinthe world. Ail who take For He in these en-\ncounters will have to...",
