    localCopyEdited: "images/articles/image-732.jpg",
    localCopyFull: "images/articles/image-732b.jpg",
    id: "732",
    text: "] 664 99\nPADDY RYAN’S “GUFE.\n. a\nHE BLOWS ABOUT CROSSING THE ATLANTIC\nTO FIGHT JEM SMITH.\n\nPlenty of Chances for Him at Home—Arthur\nChambers’ Fistic and Other Attractions—\nThe Dumb-Bell Exercise—Jack Fogarty\nand Joe Illingsworth—Sporting Gossip.\n\nSpecial Correspondence of the PosT-DIsPATCH.\n\nPHILADELPHIA, May 27.—It is reported that\nPaddy Ryan thinks of crossing the briny to\nmake a match with Jem Smith, to come off in\nIreland. I don’t think Paddy has any such\nidea but if he has he should dismiss it from his\nmind. Apart from the fact that it is extremely\ndoubtful if he could fight Smith in Ireland,\nthere remains another back of it which should\nrestrain him, and that is that he is physically\nincapable of fighting any fairly good man with\nany hopes of success. When he became rupt-\nured he should have retired from the ring.\nHe then could have done so with something of\nareputation. He had outlasted Joe Goss, who\nhad been dubbed Champion of America be-\ncause the gang back of him had robbed Tom\nAllen out of the fight he had with him at\nWalton, Ky., and so had obtained the title for\nhim. He never had a ghostof a show with\nSullivan at Mississippi City, and the flurry he\nmade with him at Madison Square Garden was\nall bounce. He was informed that the instant\nthere was ashow of slugging the fight would\nbe stopped and the affair lasted just thirty-\nfour seconds.\n\nPADDY’S CHANCES HERE.\n\nHe need not go across the water to obtain a\nfight. Dominick McCaffrey is very peacefully\ninclined...",
