    text: "gem Allen Has 2 Word to Say About Jem |\n\nsmith—Chat with President Spalding of\n\n: chicago—Sports of All Sorts—Base-Ball\nNews and Gossip-\n\nThe recent freedom with which challenges\nfor championships have been issued has pro-\nyoxed considerable discussion affecting the\nstanding ef championships in general. In a\nconversation touching the championships of\npugilism and how they have been won, the\nveteran Tom Kelly said: ‘‘Thereis the alleged\nqpampionship for middle-weights. You hear\nagreat deal  f talk about itand you see how\nthis and that fighter is matched tofight some-\npody else for it. Well, the ‘middle-\nweight championship’ means nothing.\nIt is an empty title; has no belt attached to it\nand it has never been foughtfor. Jack Demp-\nacy is called the middle-weight champion but\nhe is no more 80 than Burke who can fight at\nmiddle-weight or Mitchell who can do the\nsame thing. Sullivan can be properly be\ncalled the heavy-weight champion of Amer-\ntea, for the reason that he whipped Ryan at\nMississippi City when Ryan held that title and\nthe fight was for the title. The belts that fly\nground the country for the middle-weight\njight-weight and heavy-weight cham-\npionships are mo more worthy than\n\nany pelt that anybody can go out and buy and\n\noffer. All fights for the championship must be\naccording to London geogptes. 3 rules, with\npare fists, and any fight for a championship\nunder any other rules will not legally entitle\nthe winner toit. The Queensberry rules were\nmade for gentlemen...",
