    text: "Arresting the Fighters.\n\nIn the arrests under the prize-fighting warrants\nfor the McManus#Flint fight, mentiondd elsewhere,\nthe veteran Tom Allen was the first to be caught in\nthe net, as he expressed it. Mewasarrested a few\nminutes before noon, —_ as he was about to sit down\nto breakfast. The sheriff took him to the Four\nCourts, where he gave bond for his —— at\nUnion, Frankiin Co., in the court of Justice ay |\nFrazee at 10 o'clock to-morrow morning. The bond\nwasinthe sum of $500. Next came Jim, or Rusty\nEvans, who keeps ascaloon on Market street. After\nthe bond had been drawn up he sald he guessed a\nmistake had been made, and tliat Jim Evans of Kan-\nses City, trainer of McManus, was the party\nwanted. He was held noti] the matter\ncould be examined and it could be\ndefinitely ascertained whether he was the man\nwanted, he having been merely a spectator, Jake\nEsher was the next to be broughtin. He frrnished\nbond immediately. After ‘‘Rusty’’ Evans had been\nheld about an hour Deputy Sheriff ay concluded\nhe was not the oy wanted, and let_ him go, Evaus\npromising to be at his saloon if needed.\n\nTom Kelly and FP. J. Tucker were brought in at\n2 o'clock this afternoon, and were immediately re-\nleased on bond,\n\nUnion, Mo., the seat of Franklin County, is on the\nSt. Louis, Kansas City & Colorado Road, and to\nreach there at 10a. m. to-morrow the men al have\nto leave on that road at 5 o’clock this evening.",
