    id: "761",
    text: "evil IN ONE ROUND-\nTom Allen, Ex-Champion, Knocked\n| Out by Dan Daly.\n- Tom A lien, the ex-champion of the world\nwas knocked out in one round (rules barred)\nby Dan Daly, champion middle weight of\nMissouri, at an early hour yesterday morn-\ning. From statements made by a number of\nspectators it appears that about 1:30 o’clock\nyesterday morning Dan Daly was sitting\nin front of his saloon on Seventh\nstreet between Market and Chestnut streets\ntrying keep cool with the aid of a fan when\nthree men ran by, followed by Tom Allen,\nDutch Neil, Steve Hearn and Jack Ryan.\nThe fugitive disappeared around the corner\nof Seventh and Chestnut streets and the\npursuers approached Mr. Daly. Allen, who\nappeared to be very mad, claimed that one of\nthe three men who had been calling him vile\nnames, was in Daly’s saloon. Dan arose\nfrom his chair and told Allen that he must be\n| mistaken, as he neyer saw the men _ before,\nand most certainly was not hid-\ning them. Allen became infuriated,\nand, it is said, accused Dan\nof doing things to hurt his (Allen’s) business.\n| Charley Daly, Dan’s brother, who was in the\nhouse, heard the loud talking, joined those on\nthe outside and tried to pacify the irate ex-\nchampion. AJlon was not to be quieted, how-\never, and it is alleged that as soon as Charley\ninterfered he tried to strike him. Dan, who\nis much heayier than -his brother, became\nriled and threw off his coat and made for Allen.\nwhile Charley paid close attention to Neal\n| Hearn and Ryan, who were crowding...",
