    localCopyFull: "images/articles/image-764b.jpg",
    id: "764",
    text: "DEACON Hovser’s paper is 1 migtaken if it\nsupposes that there was any spirit of irrever-\nence in the Christmas questions of Tum Rr-\nPUBLIC, Or anything to justify this comment:\n\nSome of the ministers were even more emphatic\nthan those quoted, but they declined to engage in\nthe discussion of 60 sacred atheme witha man\nwhose questions seemed to indicate an absolute\nlack of faith in the Saviour of men,\n\nThis is from Deacon Hovussr’s paper of Sat-\nurday, the 8th. Deacon Hovusrr’s paper of\nFriday, the 7th, said:\n\nWhen prize-fights are arranged itis always a\nmatter of confidence between the parties, and all\nare supposed to be in earnest. If one weakens it\nis always easy to stop the fight, but it would bea\npity to stop the Daly-McManus fight when both\nthe principals are ready to proceed. Letthe mill\ngo on, by all means.\n\nNow this latter is a part of a protest against\nthe interference of Mr. Tom ALLnn with a\nprize-fight, the details of which, published in\nDeacon Hovser’s paper, would cause tho sale\nof sundry extra copies. Mr. ALten is him-\ncel? a refoemed prize-fighter and we may Bub:",
