    localCopyFull: "images/articles/image-766b.jpg",
    id: "766",
    text: "CONCERNING “SLUGGERS.’’\nCharlie Sails for ‘‘Lunnon’’—John ELE, Not\nDrunk—Fighting Tips.\n\nBy Telegraph to the PosT-DISPATCH.\n\nNEw York, January 19.—‘‘Charlie is over\nthe water and Charlie is over the sea,’’ that\nis, he ison the ‘‘briny’’ and will soon again\nbe in dear old ‘’Lunnon.’’ The »vdoxing\nchampion of England got a glorious send-off,\ntoo, Jack Dempsey’s farewell address being &\nlively one. I saw ‘‘Mister’’ Mitchell two\nnights previous to his departure, he being\nwith Al Smith and ‘‘Parson’’ Davies in Bang’s\nBroadway palace. I do not remember having\nseen Mitchell look so well on any By y\noccasion as he did then, and my wo: for it,\nhe looked big enough and able to\nwhip almost any man who wears\nshoe leather. Of course I know he won’t\nmake the attempt. He has declared himself\naverse to fighting and pleads bad hands as ap\nexcuse. Doubtiess he has bad fists, but Ido\nnot think thatis allthatails him, and I think\nthat if the truth was known Charlie is fearful\nof meeting Dempsey. Not that he would be\nafraid to fight Jack, but he knows the —\nidolize Dempsey and detest him. He willnot,\nI believe,ever meet Dempsey in the ring and all\nthat Jack can say or do will not induce him to\ngo in fora finish fight. Itis useless for Jack\nto make any more proposalsto him, and the\nbest thing he can do is to ignore the English -\nman.\n\nJOHN L.’S JAMBOREE.\n\nAccording to reports from Boston Jobn L.\nwas quietly indulging in intoxicants the past\nweek, notwithstanding his vows to remain an\nabstainer....",
