    text: "Sporting Notes.\n\nTom ALLEN, retired champion pugilist o:\nthe world, 619 Market street. Free concer\nevery evening.’ Best of singers only engagec\nhere. |\n\nTHE CRIMINAL RECORD.\n\nMade Love and Then Swindled Them.\n\nMrs. Kate Crawford, of No. 814 South Eightt\nstreet, reported to the police yesterday morn:\ning that she was robbed of $150 by a man whc\ngave his name as George Freiboth\nThe robbery was so cleverly exe.\ncuted that the police -are inclined tc\nregard it as the work of a professional ‘‘con’\nman. About two weeks ago Mrs. Crawford\nnoticed an advertisement in a|'German morn:\ning paper, in which a partner: with\nsome cash was -wanted in-a_ saloon\nand boarding house venture. Mrs. Craw-\nford answered on behalf of her daughter,\nMrs. Brown, a. widow. The’ ct states 4 day\nFreiboth called upon Mrs. Crawford. eis 8\nI eat Man about ©35 years old, €\neet in aeight, slender ‘limbed, dark\nhair and eyes, black mustache and bore\nhimself with Inilitary stiffness. He\nintroduced nimself by saying that he had just\ncome to this cityg and claithed to have re-\ncently resigned a ®ommission’ in the German\narmy. He tcld the women that he had a cash\naccount of $900. . This he did not think\nwas quite enough’ to Iaunch a successful\nBusiness, and he wished to find some one with\nas much more. Freiboth was quite an ac-\ncomplished conversationalist, and was\non friendly \\ terms ine yery\nshort whilé.' He told Mrs. Crawford\nthat he hgd secured a suitable location\nin Sguth St. Louis, and promised to call\nagaid....",
