    id: "863",
    text: "NOT GENEROUS JIM.\n| aaaineinainn a sanieieeneenRnne\n\nCorbett’s Alleged Shabby Treatment of\n\n<5 Mike Donovan.\n\nHE SENDS THE PROFESSOR A CHECK\nTHAT WAS PROMPTLY RETURNED.\nThe Man Who Risked Everything for Him\n\nGets $250 for His Pains—Starter\nJimmy Rowe’s Career—An Eastern\nWriter Scores Von Der Ahe—Gossip\n\nFrom Turf, Ring and Diamond.\n\nNew York, Sept. 20.—Taking up Jim Cor-\nbett asa protege turns out a very unsatis-\nfactory experiment for veteran Mike bono-\nvan, the boxing instructor of the New York\nAthletic Club. Whenthe Californian made\nhis first visitto the metropolis three years\nago Donovan took a fancy to him and\nthrough his influence Corbett was made a\nguest of the New York Athletic Club, an\nhonor that has fallen to no other pugilist.\nThe professor was also largely instrumental\nin getting on the Corbett-McCaffrey match\nand in other ways rendered invaluable ser-\nvices to the young stranger,\n\nWhen Corbett returned to the city after his\nbattle with Peter Jackson in San Francisco,\nthe courtesies of the New York Athletic Club\nwere again extended to htm. Prof. Donovan\nproposed the challenge to Sullivan and got\nEd Kearny and other New York Athletic Club\nmembers to put up a large share of Corbett’s\n§1,000 . stake. Mike took a prominent\nshare in making the big match, and\nsince then has looked after Corbett’s\ninterests faithfully. It was against the\nwishes of prominent officials of the New\nYork Athletic Club that Donovan went to\nNew Orleans to act as adviser in Corbett’s\ncorner,...",
