    text: ". **Parson” Davies in Chicago.\nSpecial Dispatch to the Globe-D crat.\n\nCHICAGO, ILL., November | 18.—‘*Parson’’\nDavies arrived in the city from the East to-\njay. Peter Jackson will visit Chicago about\nDecember 5-and remain pee aweek. Josepa\nChoynski will arrive about the same time\nand the pair, under Davies’ escort, will\nstart for the Pacific Slope, mpere they will\nbe tendered a joint testimonial. It~is pos-\nsible that the ‘*Parson’? may arrange an\nathletic show in Chicago. ‘*Jackson,’’ said\nthe manager, «‘‘is willing to allow Corbett\nany reasonable time ‘to | prepare for a\nfight. He does not care to go into\nthe ring until next September, but\nhe does think that he| merits some\nrecornition at Corbett’s hahds. He knows\nthat Corbett is making money and is glad of\nit. The manly thing for Corbett to do would\nbe to appoint a meeting and\\ sign\narticles for a battle eight or nine\nmonths hence. That~ ouid please\nthe public, and Peter, would be certain\nof afight. As it is, Corbett is holding off,\nand Jackson is becoming discouraged. His\nfriends tell him that Corbettjhas no idea of\nmeeting him. Peter is 31 years old, and he\nrealizes that he is not growing batten. He\nWants this affair@off his mind. He fought\nadraw with Corbett and Corbett has given it\nout that he wants to meet him and settle up\nold scores. Before the big fights in New Or-\nleans [announced that, win or lose, Jackson\nwould meet Corbett. You will remember that\nthe papers ‘printed an alleged letter from\nMike Donoyan te Tom...",
