    id: "876",
    text: "CRIMSON AND BLUE.\n—_——— oo\nThe Rival Colleges Meet To-Day at\nSpringfield. :\nCHARLEY MITCHELL WRITES TOM ALLEN\nA CHARACTERISTIC LETTER.\nHe Says Corbett Will Strike a Surprise\nParty Before the Tenth Round—Char-\nley’s Version of His Troubles—Gossip\nofthe Pugilists—Turf Topics—General\nSporting News.\nNEw York, Nov. 19.—The sixty days’ reign\nof foot-ballas king of sports is nearing Its\nend. Foot-ball enthusiasts have no eye\njust now for anything but the great game to-\nday in Hampden Park, when Yale and Har.\nvard will lock horns. The game will be o!\nextraordinary interest to the Princeton\neleven, who will tackle the blues on Man-\nhattan Field Thanksgiving Day. The tigers\nare practicing with a vengeance for the fray,\nand they meanto wipe out Pennsylvania’s\ndefeat If it is withinthe bounds of possibility.\nThe Princeton boys will attend the Yale-\nHarvard match, and then return to Nassau’s\ncam pus and see if they can master the tricks\nwhich they may have seen the Yales work.\nYale will probably not use the same signals\nin her game with Harvard that she has pre-\npared for the Princeton game, as there might\nbe a chance to block some of their combina-\ntions.\nThe Greggains-Costello battle, which will\noccur on Monday,Nov. 28,at the Co_ey Island\nAthietic Cinb, promises to bs one of the\nmost famous that hasever been decided in\nthe stakeless ring of the club by the sea.\nBoth men are masters of the art of boxing\nand each aspires to the middle-weight cham-\npionship of the world. The winner will...",
