    text: "Tom Allen says he doesn’t know the oa\nprinciple of bull fighting; he couldn't a Rr\nnize a bull fight if it came up and shook\nhands with him. Wut he believes that any\nso-called sport that calls for dead horses\nand bulls is no sport at all.\n\n“Blow me if I wouldn't rawther go out\nto the slaughter ‘ouse on killin’ day than\nsee one of the bull fights they ‘ave down\nthere,”’ said the ex-champion. “I was goin’\nfown to see the fights, but Jim ‘All wrote\nme an’ said I would be a sucker to put up\nme com an’ take chances on gettin’ th’\ncame deal that wus put up at ‘Ot Springs.\nlm glad f stayed ‘ome now, but 1 thought\nfur a Jang time that any country that went\nfoosee a bull fight after a mass on a bleed-\nity Sunday would never kick on a niece\njuiet fight. Wot's th’ world comin’ to, any\now? In th’ old days we used to git up an\nslam at one another before a crowd that\nwould eut a throat as quick as they would\npick a pocket. I've never thought of goin’\non th’ staige in my days. We wanted to\nfsht, Th’ bloody papers do all the fightin’\nnow, Instead ef th’ fighters doin’ it. We\nrpever used to tight in th’ papers. If we\nlidu't Nght th’ papers roasted us. But\nthis guy that got so chinnmy with Johnnell\ndown there, this Menican Governor that\nsayS @ fight is brutal, an’ allows a lot of\nren to git up an’ slaughter a bull or so\nvery Sunday an’ calls it sport, makes me\nsick.\n\n“Chever see a bull fight? queried Dutch\nNeal when asked to give his opinion of the\nbrutal aspeqt of the Mexican national...",
