    text: "| In UPON HIM,\nHe EN oe |\nAND WHEN HE DID JOE ¢ rienced\nWAS A REATEN PUGILIST.\neee |\nTom Allen Says That Peter Had a\nWalkover—Pugilistie Gossip\n\nof Gotham,\n\nTom Allen, the veteran ex-champion pu-\ngilist of America, returned from New York }\nlast night. He went to Gotham to take\nin the Maher-Choynski fight at Tom |\nO’Rourke’s Broadway Club Monday night. |\nIn the Broadway Club arena each con-\ntestant is allowed one attendant. This po- |\nsition {s generally assigned to an active\nhandler, thus doing away with the old ring ;\ncustom of having a corner full of advisers.\nbehind each fighter. The Maher party were\nanxious to have Allen on hand te advise\nPeter and a special seat was reserved for\nhim at the ring side. He was in close com-\nmunication with the big Irishman through+\nout the battle, and was given great credit\nby Maher's friends fer the clever style of\n\naction he mapped out. In conversation with\n| a Republe representative last night, Alen\n| talked interestingly of the fight and other\npugiistic matters of public concern, |\n| “Peter was the most confldent fighter I\n| have ever seen enter the ring,” said the\n| Veterans. “On the other hand, Choynski\n-was just the opposite. Maher had him\n| beat from the start. The Californian landed\na great deal oftener in the first three\n} rounds, but his blows lacked steam and\nwere ineffective. Maher was eager to close\n| on him, but we all advised him to take his\ntime. Choynski was as active as a cat,\nbut he wore himseif out completely, and\n|...",
