    text: "NK SLAVIN\n\nOF FRA ,\n\n| SR\n\nTHE MAN WHO WANTED TO MEET\n\n| JOHN L. SULLIVAN BEATEN BY\nAN USNHKNOWN NEGRO.\n\nSpeed of Race Horses, Jack Rabbits\nand Greyhounds Discussed—\nSporting Gossip.\n\nFrank Slavin, the burly Australian pu-\neilist, has seen his best days. At one time\nhe appeared to have a great future before\nhim in the ring, but ever since his fight with\nPeter Jackson tn Londan, which resulted in\na victory for the giant black, Slavin has\nexperienced nothing but reverses... Slavin\nwas one of Jackson's pupiis in the Anti-\npodes, afid after Peter came to America he\nclaimed the Australian championship. No-\nbody disputed his claim until he followed\nJackson to this country. Sullivan was still\nthe American champion when Slavin ar-\nrived, end Frank endeavored to arrange a\nbattle with the Boston boy.\n\nHe came tp St. Louis to see Sullivan about\nthe matter, and John J. told him that he\nwould fight nobody until after his trip to\nAustralia. Slavin and Mitchell then toured\nthe United States, the former posing as the\nAustralian champion, notwithstanding the\nfact that Jackson was also claiming the\nsame title. The result of the controversy\nwas the fight that tock place in London,\nwhich settled Slavin's hash, as far as the\nAustralian or any other championship was\nconcerned. Slavin’s history since then is of\nlittle interest to the public, beyond some\nfacts in connection with his recent defeat\n‘at the hands of Bob Armstrong, “Parson”\nDavies’ big black.\n\nTom Allen, the retired champion,...",
