    text: "General Sporting Gossip.\n\n—The Western Illincis Trap Shooters’ League\nhas organized, with the election of the following\nofficers: President, E, E, Baker, Kewanee; sec-\nretary and treasurer, Robert H, Lamb, Kewanee;\ncaptain, H. KR. Harris, Galesburg. Monmouth,\nCanton, Kewanee, and Neponset teams were rep-\nresented. It was decided to invite Peoria, Rock\nIceland, Kelthsburg, Pekin, Mendota, Aledo and\nGalva clubs to jcin. The first tournament will\nbe held at Moumouth, June 24, and afterward a\ntournament will be held each month.\n\n—J. Lewis Holland, the crack St. Louts sprinter,\nhas gone into training and will probably make\nhis first ae tego os this season at the Hibernian\ngames, which take place at the Fair Grounds.\nHoliand is thought to be the fastest runner in\nthe West. He gave the famous John V. Crum,\nwho died recently, quite an argument at 100 yards\nshortly after Crum went East two years nae to\ntule part in the international championships,\nHolland is said te have as much speed as ever.\nHis trainer says he ran 10) yards in :10% in a\ntrial at Creve Coeur Lake Sunday.\n\n—‘‘Parson’’ Davies while in New York last\nweek offered to bet W. A. Brady $5,000 to 44.900\nthat Joe Choynski could peat James J. Corbett,\nand ‘'Pompadour Jim’s’’ backer declined, saying:\n“Corbett will fight no one but Fitzsimmons.’’\nDavies offered to match Jimmy Barry against\nDave Sullivan, agreeing that the champion han-\ntam should scale at ll0.pounds and allow Sulll-\nVan two pounds. He also cailed at the...",
