    text: "‘Denver Ed” and Paddy Smith Staying\nUp Early and Rising Late.\n\nPrize fighters, when they are not in train-\ning. are not the earliest to bed and earliest\nto rise people. “Denver Ed\" Smith was\nsleeping away at noon Tuesday, dreaming\nprobably of some of his former battles in\nthe ring. Since he was last in St. Lous\nSmith has made the tour ef the world, and\nhas fought two important matches, both of\nwhich he lost. In California he was beaten\nby Choynski, and in Australa he met and\nWas defeated by the Barrier champion, Joe\nGoddard. But he wants a return maten\nwith either of those fighters, and if he 1s\nable to connect, Tom Allen of this city\nwill back him to the extent of $2,000,\n\nAt Tom Allea's place, on Market street,\nthe two Smiths and the Belfast Spider, Ike\nWeir, heid a reception Monday pight, and\nthe festivities were Kept up until 2 o'clock\nTuesday morn ng. “Denver Ed” Smith\nbrought something of @ roll back with him\nfrom his trip to tye Antipodes, and he went\nto the Fair Grounds Tuesday aftenoon te\nee the bookmakers a try at it. His\n\nother, Patty, who leaves a for Call.\n\nfornia, where he will be matched ior o\nfight with “Yeung Corbett.” went to the\nraces with him They will both a. to Hor\nSprings at the end of this week. ke Weir.\n| who !s considered by most people a has.\njp been, has a backer in Boston, and is eur for\nany Kind of @ ght he can geu\n\n;\n=",
