    id: "964",
    text: "ee ee\n\n_ ALLEN AGAIN IN THE RING.\n\n| ie |\n\nGoes Six Rounds Every Afternoon\nWith the Bookmakers.\n\nThe latest convert to the game at the\nFair Grounds is Tom Allen, the ex-cham-\npion heavy-weight pugilist of the world.\n\nHe has always been a sporting man, but\nthe conqueror of Mike McCool has confined\nhis operations to things that can talk. For\nthe first time this season he went to the\ntrack last Saturday to see the Derby run,\nand he fell in love with the game. Now he\nis a regular.\n\nThe retired champion believes in being\nconspicuous and he dresses flashier than\nany bookmaker’s clerk or tout at the track.\nOne day he wears an immaculate white\nflannel suit, im striking contrast to his\ndyed jet black mustache, and the next day\nappears in a linen suit with tremendous—\nred and yellow checks. The band’s music\ncannot be heard when Allen, with a pair of\nglasses slung jauntily over his shoulder,\nparades up and down the grand stand. |\n\nOe AEB MN WL isn 2",
    summary: "The St. Louis Post-Dispatch reported that Tom Allen, the ex-champion heavyweight pugilist, had become a regular visitor to the Fair Grounds race track, attending the Derby and dressing in flashy clothing that drew attention.",
