    text: "About 200 people were present and nine\nprizes were awarded. The club has been in\nexistence one year, and Thursday night's\naffair turned out to be a success socially\nand financially. They would like to receive\nchallenges from other clubs. Address all\ncommunications to Joseph Peetz, 1827 Ore-\ngon avenue.\neS\nA VERY QUEER MINISTER.\nOne Who Believes in Boxing, but Who\nIs Opposed to Football.\n\nIn a sermon at Indianapolis Sunday a\nMethodist minister roasted football and up-\nheld pugilistic encounters. He had this to\nsay of McCoy’s performance there:\n\n“Now for Mr. ‘Kid’ McCoy's exhibition.\nTwo men at a time were pitted — each\nother, both wearing gloves of the bulk of\nsmall pillows, boxing according to well un-\n\n| derstood rules, under the eye of a man of\ncourage and vigilance; no foul play; every-\nthing being fair and in full view; nobody\nhurt; no doctors; nobody killed or crippled.\nIt is said that the show was the real thing.\nIf prize fighting was meant it was not ‘tbe\n| real thing.’ The real thing is a fight to a\n) finish with the naked fists, such fights as\nMike McCool and Tom Allen and John Mor-\nrissey, John €. Heenan and Jen Mace used\n| to indulge in, which were clear kin to the\npresent college football game, but which\n| bore little or no resemblance to the ‘set-\n| tos’ at Tomlinson Hall. I have no apology\n| to make for witnessing that exhibition. It\n| Was a manilier and cleaner show than one-\n| half of the football games we have had in\n| this city during the last ten years,...",
