    text: "Joe Goddard, the famous barrier cham-\npien of Australia, is now a full-fledged bex-\ning manager at Philadelphia. He is the\nmatehmaker of the Industrial Athletic\nClub at the Quaker City. Boxing is on the\nboom in Philadetphia, and Geddard ex-\npects to make big money with his elub.\nThe Maher-Rublin six-round bout attracted\n# &$6.08) house in PhiladeIpbia the other\nnight. Rubhlin’'s shure ef the gate was\n$1.90). Goddard was at one time «a prom-\ninert candidate for the  heavy-weight\nchamplonsbip of the woric. He first sprang\ninto prominence when he knocked out Joe\nChovnerki twice in suceessien. Choynski\nwent to Australia after his last fight with\nSim Corbett at San Frenciveo. The first\ntime he met Goddard they fought font\nwhiriwind rounds. Both men were all\nbut out when Goddard got in a lucky\npunch and finished Choynski. It wae the\nsame case the second time they fought.\nGoddard winning again in the fourth round.\nAfter this fight tioddard came to this coun-\ntry and met “Denver Fa” Smith at New\nOrleans. Tom Allen coached and seconded\nSmith in this fight. Goddard was an over-\nwhelming favorite at odds-on in the bet-\nting. but Smith put him out after a des-\nperate fight. After that Goddard struck\nthe pugilistic toboggan and has not been\nheard of much since.",
